{
  "dom_id": "step-q184507",
  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Let $I=[0,1]⊂R$ and ${X}_{i}=[0,2]\\times [-i,0].$ Which of the following represents ${⋂}_{i\\in I}{X}_{i}?$",
  "worked_solution": "Recall that the intersection of a family of indexed sets consists of those elements that belong to *all* the sets:\n\n$$\n{⋂}_{i\\in I}{A}_{i}=\\{x\\,:\\,x\\in {A}_{k}\\,\\,\\text{for all}\\,\\,k\\in I\\}\n$$\n\nLet's now write down one of our indexed sets. For example, if $i=0.5,$ we have \n\n$$\n{X}_{0.5}=[0,2]\\times [-0.5,0]=\\{(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in [0,2],b\\in [-0.5,0]\\}.\n$$\n\nThis represents a rectangle whose vertices are at $(0,0),$ $(2,0),$ $(2,-0.5),$ and $(0,-0.5)$ in the coordinate plane, as shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14167512/assets/5837864bfcc40e680cf62b43c0e3d145ba05b1f25e1ccae2f4788902d030d927.png)\n\nIn general,\n\n$$\n{X}_{i}=[0,2]\\times [-i,0]=\\{(a,b)\\,:\\,a\\in [0,2],b\\in [-i,0]\\}\n$$\n\nis the rectangle whose vertices are at $(0,0),$ $(2,0),$ $(2,-i),$ and $(0,-i).$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14167512/assets/f0c20436f03db4b0003d087827cefbd76506af423da3f0a3042082b5afeb4b58.png)\n\nThe intersection of all these rectangles is the line segment $[0,2]\\times \\{0\\}:$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14167512/assets/236d10f31265b400036e1ddeafa122991bcae1ea878af8b300003fb11acfa85b.png)",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
